# Generated from: specs/20-generate-recurring-shift-series-in-local-civil-time/requirements.md
Feature: Generate recurring shift series in local civil time
  As a volunteer coordinator
  I want to define a regular service position once and generate future occurrences safely
  So that weekly meetings do not require repetitive UTC data entry

  @SCN001
  Scenario Outline: Series generates bounded concrete occurrences
    Given the group IANA time zone is configured
    And a coordinator previews a <pattern> series with a 12-week horizon
    When the coordinator confirms creation
    Then actual upcoming local dates and roles become unique unpublished concrete shifts
    And each occurrence records its series revision and local date
    And a daily worker idempotently maintains the bounded horizon

    Examples:
      | pattern                                      |
      | daily every 2 days                           |
      | every 2 weeks on Monday and Thursday         |

  @SCN002
  Scenario Outline: DST start exceptions never disappear silently
    Given a series generates a local start at a daylight-saving <condition>
    When the occurrence is reconciled
    Then the occurrence <result>
    And its elapsed duration is added after start UTC is resolved

    Examples:
      | condition | result                                                                    |
      | overlap   | uses the stored first or second occurrence choice                         |
      | gap       | remains visible as Needs review without a concrete shift                  |

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Coordinator explicitly resolves a gap
    Given one occurrence is Needs review because its local start does not exist
    When the coordinator previews and chooses a valid replacement local time
    Then one unpublished concrete shift is created as an exception
    And adjacent occurrences are unchanged
    When another gap occurrence is skipped with a reason
    Then it remains visible and audited without a shift

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Future correction protects live commitments by default
    Given a new effective revision reaches eligible, protected, and manually changed future occurrences
    When the coordinator confirms the ordinary series correction
    Then eligible non-exceptions adopt the revision
    And protected occurrences keep their prior shifts and workflow as detached exceptions
    And manual exceptions remain unchanged
    And resolving a protected occurrence requires a separate issue-13 consequence confirmation

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Selected horizon publication is all or nothing
    Given reviewed generated occurrences are selected by local-date range
    And one selected occurrence is stale or Needs review
    When the coordinator confirms publication
    Then no selected shift is published
    And every blocking local date and plain-language reason is shown
    When every selected occurrence is eligible with current versions
    Then all selected shifts and audits commit in one transaction

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Group-zone change pauses series generation
    Given the group zone changes while an active series retains its prior IANA zone snapshot
    When daily top-up runs
    Then no new occurrence is generated for that series
    And coordinator home reports Zone review required
    When the coordinator previews and confirms adopting the group zone
    Then a new effective revision records the decision
    And protected and exception UTC shifts remain fixed
    And bounded top-up resumes under the new zone
